#| Lines beginning "#|" are notes to us and are stripped by render.sh. Everything else is
#| the manifest a winget-pkgs moderator reads, and it is kept short on purpose: rationale
#| belongs in packaging/winget/README.md, not in a file submitted to someone else's repo.
#|
#| InstallerType: zip + NestedInstallerType: portable
#|     Boks is a CLI, and the Windows artifact is a bundle rather than a lone binary: the
#|     CLI ships beside containerd, the nerdbox shim, krun.dll and the guest images,
#|     because Boks orchestrates a stack it does not contain. A zip is the only archive
#|     type winget unpacks, and `portable` is the only nested type that suits a CLI.
#|
#| No ArchiveBinariesDependOnPath
#|     Setting it true would put the whole extracted directory on the user's PATH —
#|     containerd.exe, ctr.exe, mkfs.erofs.exe and mkfs.ext4.exe included, shadowing a
#|     containerd the user installed on purpose. Leaving it unset does NOT reliably avoid
#|     that, and saying it did was this file's mistake. winget's own documentation states
#|     the fallback: unset or false "will use the default behavior of adding a symlink to
#|     the links folder, if supported, or adding the install location directly to PATH if
#|     symlinks are not supported" (doc/manifest/schema/1.12.0/installer.md). On 2026-08-16
#|     symlinks were NOT supported on the test machine — Developer Mode off, unelevated,
#|     `SYMLINK REFUSED: Administrator privilege required` — so winget took the second
#|     branch and put this directory on the User PATH. Three other winget packages on that
#|     machine were on PATH the same way, so it is winget's ordinary unprivileged outcome
#|     rather than one machine's quirk.
#|
#|     Unset is still the right value, because it is the only one that lets a machine which
#|     CAN make symlinks get the clean outcome; true would force the shadowing everywhere.
#|     But the honest description is "one alias where symlinks work, the whole directory on
#|     PATH where they do not", and the second case is the common one. The real fix is an
#|     archive layout change, not a field here: winget adds
#|     `symlinkTargetPath.parent_path()` — the directory holding the nested exe — so a
#|     `bin/boks.exe` beside `libexec/boks/` would put only `bin/` on PATH. See
#|     packaging/winget/README.md; it is not done at 0.1.1 because the published archive is
#|     flat and this manifest must describe the archive that exists.
#|
#|     None of this affects Boks finding its own runtime: internal/daemon/locate.go resolves
#|     the running executable, follows symlinks, and searches the directory it lands in, and
#|     on 2026-08-16 every runtime path resolved inside the winget package directory.
#|
#| MinimumOSVersion: 10.0.22000.0
#|     Windows 11 RTM. The Windows Hypervisor Platform predates it, but Windows 11 is the
#|     only thing this stack has ever been run on (docs/verification.md), so this is the
#|     floor we can state rather than the floor that might work.
#|
#| x64 only
#|     There is no Windows arm64 build. libkrun's WHP backend here is x86_64, and so is the
#|     guest kernel that has booted under it.
#|
#| RelativeFilePath uses a FORWARD slash, deliberately
#|     Merged manifests use both. BurntSushi.ripgrep.MSVC 14.1.1 writes a backslash;
#|     sharkdp.fd 10.4.2 — ManifestVersion 1.12.0, written by komac, merged 2026-03 — writes
#|     a forward slash. The forward slash is also what the archive's own central directory
#|     contains, which is what the zip format requires. `winget install --manifest` accepted
#|     it on 2026-08-16. Do not "correct" this to a backslash.
#|
#| Field order follows the JSON schema's own property order — Platform and MinimumOSVersion
#| come BEFORE InstallerType, which is not where this file used to put them. Same reasoning
#| as the locale manifest: nothing rejects the other order, but every tool that might ever
#| rewrite this manifest emits the schema order.
# Created by packaging/winget/render.sh in github.com/dagsommer/boks
# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://aka.ms/winget-manifest.installer.1.12.0.schema.json

PackageIdentifier: dagsommer.boks
PackageVersion: {{VERSION}}
Platform:
- Windows.Desktop
MinimumOSVersion: 10.0.22000.0
InstallerType: zip
NestedInstallerType: portable
Commands:
- boks
ReleaseDate: {{RELEASE_DATE}}
Installers:
- Architecture: x64
  NestedInstallerFiles:
  - RelativeFilePath: boks_{{VERSION}}_windows_amd64/boks.exe
    PortableCommandAlias: boks
  InstallerUrl: https://github.com/dagsommer/boks/releases/download/v{{VERSION}}/boks_{{VERSION}}_windows_amd64.zip
  InstallerSha256: {{INSTALLER_SHA256}}
ManifestType: installer
ManifestVersion: 1.12.0
